WEBVTT

00:03.960 --> 00:05.790
<b>This was another episode-</b>

00:05.900 --> 00:07.690
<b>That didn't have a conclusion.</b>

00:08.270 --> 00:11.060
<b>You go, ''Oh. What?''
And that's it.</b>

00:12.970 --> 00:17.870
<b>It ends without finding out
who the fake Dejiko is.</b>

00:17.980 --> 00:19.940
<b>That's true.</b>

00:21.750 --> 00:26.180
<b>So I asked them,
''What does it mean?''</b>

00:26.280 --> 00:28.410
<b>But they told me,
''The mystery is good.</b>

00:29.020 --> 00:32.050
<b>The fake Dejiko might be
somewhere in the world still.</b>

00:32.690 --> 00:34.160
<b>That's what's good.''</b>

00:34.860 --> 00:38.060
<b>No one would think that.</b>

00:38.700 --> 00:41.060
<b>But it made us think.</b>

00:41.200 --> 00:43.690
<b>We never had
any qualms about these.</b>

00:44.400 --> 00:45.800
<b>We just thought, ''I see.''</b>

00:45.800 --> 00:47.000
<b>We just thought, ''I see.''</b>

00:48.140 --> 00:51.170
<b>This is the episode that's considered
the best, ''Warm, Fluffy Rice.''</b>

00:52.780 --> 00:56.740
<b>I wonder
how the U.S. fans feel</b>

00:57.350 --> 01:01.050
<b>about this type of surreal episode.</b>

01:07.660 --> 01:11.150
<b>I think, to theJapanese,
this strange feeling was-</b>

01:11.700 --> 01:13.860
<b>They felt peaceful?</b>

01:15.400 --> 01:17.870
<b>When they first saw it,
it was like ''huh?''</b>

01:17.970 --> 01:21.930
<b>But as they saw it over and over again,
it got to them.</b>

01:23.270 --> 01:27.070
<b>I don't know how
the fans here will react.</b>

01:28.080 --> 01:32.450
<b>I don't remember if I heard
a lot about this episode, though.</b>

01:35.690 --> 01:38.660
<b>Who designed the yukata?</b>

01:38.760 --> 01:41.950
<b>The one with all the ''de?''</b>

01:42.060 --> 01:43.720
<b>Probably Yamakawa-san.</b>

01:44.400 --> 01:48.560
<b>We had the animation staff
handle those things.</b>

01:48.670 --> 01:50.960
<b>So the PJs were
also designed by them.</b>

01:51.070 --> 01:55.470
<b>We had them take care
of everything within the anime.</b>

01:55.570 --> 01:57.770
<b>Even this rice bowl too.</b>

01:58.340 --> 01:59.830
<b>And how one eye is open.</b>

01:59.940 --> 02:02.140
<b>I have no clue what it means.</b>

02:04.080 --> 02:07.250
<b>It's gonna be tough
explaining this to the fans.</b>

02:07.350 --> 02:09.050
<b>Really?</b>

02:09.650 --> 02:11.020
<b>Oh, yes.</b>

02:28.610 --> 02:31.730
<b>It's a lot like a dream.</b>

02:33.280 --> 02:35.510
<b>That's what makes it so interesting.</b>

02:35.610 --> 02:38.140
<b>I was there
when they recorded this episode.</b>

02:38.250 --> 02:41.910
<b>The voice actors looked puzzled too.</b>

02:42.020 --> 02:43.650
<b>As they were reading their lines?</b>

02:43.760 --> 02:46.120
<b>They had faces that said,
''What was that?''</b>

02:47.330 --> 02:52.700
<b>That thing about an old man farting.
Does that happen a lot in Japan?</b>

02:53.030 --> 02:58.090
<b>Even if it does,
you wouldn't be able to hear it.</b>

03:32.940 --> 03:35.240
<b>They have shifts, don't they?</b>

03:35.340 --> 03:37.540
<b>I guess so.</b>

03:40.350 --> 03:44.370
<b>It's hard to tell
what time she goes to work.</b>

03:44.480 --> 03:46.980
<b>When you see this,
it looks like it's pretty early.</b>
